 "scenes": [
  {
   "id": "intro",
   "steps": [
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "The scoreboard found WAR and WAW hazards, but could only stall for them. Robert Tomasulo, at IBM in 1967, removed them entirely, by renaming registers in hardware. His algorithm is the heart of every out-of-order processor today."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "write",
       "target": "head"
      },
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "head",
       "text": "Tomasulo's algorithm, part 1"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Here are the eight stages."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "stages"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "The idea, the structure, the three steps, and what a reservation station holds."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "stages[0..=3]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Then renaming watched entry by entry, how WAR and WAW disappear, a comparison with the scoreboard, and an exam question. The full cycle-by-cycle trace is the next video."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "stages[4..=7]"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "idea",
   "steps": [
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Stage 1: four ideas."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "head",
       "text": "Stage 1 of 8: the idea"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "stages"
      },
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "idea"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Each functional unit gets a set of reservation stations: buffers where instructions wait, along with their operands."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "idea[0]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "When an instruction issues, any operand that is already available is copied into its station immediately. Later writes to that register cannot disturb it."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "idea[1]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "An operand not yet available is named by the station that will produce it. That name, the tag, replaces the register name. That is renaming."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "idea[2]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "And every result is broadcast on a common data bus, with its tag. Every station waiting for that tag grabs the value at once. Forwarding comes for free."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "idea[3]"
      },
      {
       "action": "write",
       "target": "takeaway"
      },
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "takeaway",
       "text": "stations hold operands · tags replace register names · the CDB broadcasts"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "struct",
   "steps": [
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Stage 2: the structure. Instructions leave an instruction queue in order."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "head",
       "text": "Stage 2 of 8: the structure"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "takeaway"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "idea"
      },
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "dg"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "dg.iq"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Each goes to a station of the right kind: load buffers, add stations, or multiply stations, which also handle divides."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "dg.lb"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "dg.ars",
       "delay": 0.2
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "dg.mrs",
       "delay": 0.4
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "A station sends its instruction to the unit once both operands are present. So instructions execute out of order."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "dg.add"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "dg.mul",
       "delay": 0.2
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "dg.mem",
       "delay": 0.4
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Results go onto the common data bus."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "dg.cdb"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "dg.add->cdb",
       "delay": 0.2
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "dg.mul->cdb",
       "delay": 0.4
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "From the bus they reach the registers, and also every station that is waiting for them. The bus is the only path for results."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "dg.reg"
